WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:17.440
Okay guys so it's been quite a while since the first chopper episode 

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.744
And a lot of you have been asking am I still pursuing this challenge

00:00:20.744 --> 00:00:22.227
And the answer is yes

00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:25.282
But the pandemic and an injury I had hasn't made it easy.

00:00:25.282 --> 00:00:28.057
But during the last few months I have been able to practice more

00:00:28.057 --> 00:00:30.057
So now it's time for an update on my progress!

00:00:34.001 --> 00:00:36.001
Today I will be practicing irregular with Otto

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:37.844
Lets start with a short warm-up!

00:01:02.995 --> 00:01:04.138
That was perfect!

00:01:04.138 --> 00:01:06.000
Now the big reveal...

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.618
Emil is the real Sensei!

00:01:07.618 --> 00:01:09.106
All this time!

00:01:09.393 --> 00:01:10.471
Okay that was nice

00:01:10.471 --> 00:01:13.014
But unfortunately those were just some highlights

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:15.014
If we look at my chopping development

00:01:15.014 --> 00:01:17.427
I'm still doing a lot of easy mistakes

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.760
And it's hard to be consistent with the chops

00:01:24.102 --> 00:01:25.721
Yeah I shouldn't miss the first one

00:01:26.114 --> 00:01:29.150
But at the same time my chop has also improved quite a bit

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.179
There is a lot more spin in the chops right now

00:01:33.151 --> 00:01:36.503
Even the Sensei had to admit this a few times during our session!

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:38.267
Aaaah, lift it!

00:01:38.661 --> 00:01:40.194
But now let's get on to the exercise

00:01:40.194 --> 00:01:42.442
Which Otto is very kind to explain to you!

00:01:42.944 --> 00:01:44.750
Emil is going to hit to this area

00:01:45.946 --> 00:01:47.601
So Otto doesn't have to move his legs

00:01:47.601 --> 00:01:48.288
Yes!

00:01:48.288 --> 00:01:49.997
And I will hit anywhere

00:01:49.997 --> 00:01:51.774
So Emil has to move his legs!

00:01:52.508 --> 00:01:55.237
In this exercise Otto hits the first ball to my backhand

00:01:55.237 --> 00:01:56.622
And after that it's free

00:02:05.486 --> 00:02:07.050
The reason why I like this exercise

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:09.404
Is that it demonstrates a real game situation

00:02:09.404 --> 00:02:11.677
Much better than regular exersises

00:02:12.235 --> 00:02:13.377
Just like in a real match

00:02:13.377 --> 00:02:15.806
In this exercise you don't know where the ball is coming

00:02:15.806 --> 00:02:17.311
So you have to be ready for everything

00:02:21.026 --> 00:02:24.293
And even though the rallies aren't as long as in regular exercises

00:02:24.293 --> 00:02:27.912
It can be really useful for your game play to practice irregular

00:02:28.455 --> 00:02:30.226
The chop is looking quite good today Emil!

00:02:36.742 --> 00:02:37.564
Three steps:

00:02:37.564 --> 00:02:38.064
1. Chop

00:02:38.064 --> 00:02:38.691
2. Lift

00:02:38.691 --> 00:02:39.479
3. Smash!

00:02:39.519 --> 00:02:40.189
Good combo!

00:02:44.893 --> 00:02:45.504
Good

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:47.217
That's my combo!

00:02:47.217 --> 00:02:48.636
That's also a good combo!

00:02:49.552 --> 00:02:53.000
If we look at a few things that I clearly need to improve a lot more

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.695
The first thing is my footwork

00:02:56.822 --> 00:02:58.336
You are way too far away

00:02:58.336 --> 00:02:59.469
Yeah it seems so

00:02:59.469 --> 00:03:01.002
You should take a step closer

00:03:03.146 --> 00:03:06.089
In many situations I'm staying too far away from the ball

00:03:06.089 --> 00:03:07.830
So I'm not able to do a proper shot

00:03:11.696 --> 00:03:14.651
I think most of your mistakes come when you don't move enough

00:03:14.651 --> 00:03:17.439
You really have to be on the top of your feet

00:03:17.439 --> 00:03:19.952
So you really have to get your body behind the ball

00:03:19.952 --> 00:03:22.292
If you compare the previous shot with this one

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:26.263
You can see that by taking just a small adjusting move

00:03:26.263 --> 00:03:28.262
I'm able to make a much better shot

00:03:29.028 --> 00:03:30.382
The second problem that I noticed

00:03:30.382 --> 00:03:34.000
Was the difficulty to be in the right starting position for the next shot

00:03:34.619 --> 00:03:36.159
I didn't really know should I be ready

00:03:36.159 --> 00:03:39.158
To take the next shot with my backhand or my forehand

00:03:39.954 --> 00:03:41.223
And as you see in these clips

00:03:41.223 --> 00:03:43.404
I was too often waiting with the wrong side 

00:03:45.632 --> 00:03:46.811
In that especially

00:03:46.811 --> 00:03:48.722
You were waiting for the forehand

00:03:48.722 --> 00:03:49.560
Then I hit to your backhand

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:50.675
It's hard to chop

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:53.913
So I think you should be more ready for the backhand

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.876
More like somehow here 

00:04:03.902 --> 00:04:04.845
Now it helped!

00:04:05.567 --> 00:04:08.088
It's really hard but it feels that I would need to find some

00:04:08.088 --> 00:04:11.571
Golden middle way to be ready on both sides after every shot

00:04:13.467 --> 00:04:14.667
Now I was in the wrong!

00:04:15.682 --> 00:04:17.404
It's not as simple as it looks!
No it's not!

00:04:18.574 --> 00:04:20.460
The third thing that felt really difficult

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:23.031
was to hit a no spin ball after doing some chops

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:29.138
The problem here is that the long pimple rubber reacts very differently

00:04:29.138 --> 00:04:32.087
To a hard spin ball compared to a no spin ball

00:04:37.702 --> 00:04:39.540
It's so different when there is no spin!

00:04:40.001 --> 00:04:42.125
Yeah you haven't really practiced that yet

00:04:49.015 --> 00:04:49.948
That was good!

00:04:50.479 --> 00:04:51.460
Surprisingly good!

00:04:52.416 --> 00:04:54.000
That was a good chop from the no spin

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:55.257
Yeah that was good

00:04:55.666 --> 00:04:56.723
That's the right way

00:04:57.345 --> 00:05:00.564
All in all it feels that I have definitely improved from the first episode

00:05:00.564 --> 00:05:02.161
And chopping feels better now

00:05:02.161 --> 00:05:04.365
But there is obviously still so much to learn

00:05:04.365 --> 00:05:06.422
To get things right with this playing style

00:05:06.422 --> 00:05:08.734
It just requires a lot more practice.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:09.878
Thanks!

